            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0215" n="99" xml:id="pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/487.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to France to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-06-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 28, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Acting Secretary for Foreign Affairs today confirmed protest of Japan and Russia
                    against Article 16. French Foreign Office preparing memorandum recommending
                    entire suppression of this article, because it relates only to future business,
                    does not affect present loan, and would virtually create a monopoly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bacon</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
